4T15:33:22", "owner": "alex__s.j", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18077349791323038, "text": "Where can I watch the full video? 🤣", "created_at": "2025-11-14T13:56:04", "owner": "rudy_sempai", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18076388642216924, "text": "可育种", "created_at": "2025-11-14T08:33:10", "owner": "i.am.azrael0__0", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18120360073523546, "text": "“Now go hit the pentagon, Murr.”", "created_at": "2025-11-14T03:42:26", "owner": "owen_cass622", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17928664389117965, "text": "😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-13T12:00:29", "owner": "josefcords", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18133275112467591, "text": "😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-13T10:15:41", "owner": "baba_gautam_baral", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18083169418846184, "text": "", "created_at": "2025-11-13T07:29:42", "owner": "yanki_arici", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17933262174105071, "text": "זה כל כך קשוח.", "created_at": "2025-11-12T22:50:13", "owner": "king_of_tapeworms", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17969965250816554, "text": "😂😂😂😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-12T18:53:04", "owner": "artamohamadio", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18059541767215361, "text": "", "created_at": "2025-11-12T16:16:48", "owner": "rishiisobese", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17988888551905691, "text": "@manveshkajale", "created_at": "2025-11-12T08:29:20", "owner": "pranshhii", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18083706500006573, "text": "Og family friendly @familyfriendlyog", "created_at": "2025-11-12T06:18:03", "owner": "max.wiseman113", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18074027963195480, "text": "😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-12T03:13:15", "owner": "ztx_obito", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18143289172445839, "text": "❤️❤️❤️❤️❤️❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-12T02:51:38", "owner": "hotel._carlota", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18053840291324123, "text": "", "created_at": "2025-11-11T19:57:42", "owner": "witrotay_", "likes": 12}, {"id": 17914753932212198, "text": "😂", "created_at": "2025-11-11T17:08:27", "owner": "carmelite_mohak.op", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18029922533548476, "text": "Alright", "created_at": "2025-11-11T16:52:41", "owner": "eetupaija", "likes": 0}], "location": null, "hashtags": []},
{"media_id": 3768065028017146612, "shortcode": "DRK2y3NiMr0", "permalink": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DRK2y3NiMr0/", "taken_at": "2025-11-17T19:42:00", "caption": "The classic midday meal.  #british #britishicon #britishculture #britishlife #britishfood #mealdeal #mealdeals", "owner_username": "theotherbritishmuseum", "owner_id": "71953226431", "likes": 19998, "is_video": true, "typename": "GraphVideo", "media": [{"type": "video", "path": "0016_DRK2y3NiMr0\\DRK2y3NiMr0_20251117_194200.mp4"}], "comments": [{"id": 18080557559142953, "text": "the shock when I moved from Brazil to England and found out this was considered lunch 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-20T13:55:53", "owner": "annssantos", "likes": 453}, {"id": 18367115716084822, "text": "How did i work at boots head office for 5 years and not know they invented the meal deal?", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:02:22", "owner": "drunkatthehelm", "likes": 45}, {"id": 17934600339109967, "text": "😮😍🙌", "created_at": "2025-12-16T10:19:09", "owner": "angelaaachy", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18059805920640314, "text": "The meal deal saved us almost every day in our trip to London last October. For a family of 5 walking around to know the city, the meal deal was a great option!", "created_at": "2025-11-21T01:53:06", "owner": "melusachetto", "likes": 4}, {"id": 17936491886981830, "text": "Boots used to do a lovely chicken tikka flatbread, and a fizzy boysenberry drink in their meal deal. Good old days!", "created_at": "2025-11-24T15:09:22", "owner": "oratrixvo", "likes": 3}, {"id": 17989324322738771, "text": "£2,50 26 years ago and it's only about £4 now that's pretty good going", "created_at": "2025-11-18T10:25:11", "owner": "ushmiaster", "likes": 16}, {"id": 18096966739895086, "text": "I use to love boots meal deals 😍😍", "created_at": "2025-12-17T03:16:45", "owner": "its_pawsible_walkies", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17891224971240360, "text": "Boots still have the best meal deal", "created_at": "2025-11-22T09:38:02", "owner": "sativalikesalma", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18144583543445645, "text": "Meal deal was invented by Boots Assistant to the Regional Manager in 1856; Sir Mealy Mc Dealey when he incorrectly put a 3 for 1 sticker and the public refused to allow the error to be corrected.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T08:30:18", "owner": "ahmed_shahid.jpg", "likes": 182}, {"id": 18378135940199268, "text": "So happy to be italian 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-18T23:08:20", "owner": "marco0piras", "likes": 154}, {"id": 17891492427368513, "text": "It’s the most depressing lunch I can imagine", "created_at": "2025-11-21T11:21:22", "owner": "yaron.einav", "likes": 7}, {"id": 17903793546301414, "text": "😂😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-30T02:23:57", "owner": "radiantnavin", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17985721331919796, "text": "This information should be part of the Life in The UK test. 😂❤️", "created_at": "2025-12-17T11:30:23", "owner": "manololpez", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18074963531191805, "text": "It took off during the 80s because lunch at home had stopped being a thing with women having a significant presence in the workforce and more people eating their lunch at their desk. More labour and less leisure leads to increased demand for convenience foods", "created_at": "2025-11-18T07:27:59", "owner": "janellelizabeth89", "likes": 122}, {"id": 17955291093035091, "text": "Boots used to do a Mexican sarney with cheese and I don’t know what …I loved it …I think they ran a competition to invent new sandwich fillers !!", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:05:40", "owner": "mzfit123", "likes": 10}, {"id": 18330316756241925, "text": "Landing at Heathrow the other day I knew I was home when walking past Boots I saw those two words!", "created_at": "2025-12-04T20:18:03", "owner": "philthomas5036", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18081048929333940, "text": "I spent $15 on a sandwich today. Meal Deals are the best thing ever. Really keeps my UK travel budget down.", "created_at": "2025-11-22T06:06:09", "owner": "kiasuchick", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18044448257490252, "text": "Brilliant. But still not lunch 😂", "created_at": "2025-12-13T20:00:40", "owner": "astronaths", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18010694606806243, "text": "I travelled for a few weeks in the UK this summer and loved the meal deal! I’ve been telling my friends how essential it was to my travels!!! 😆 So funny!", "created_at": "2025-11-21T07:02:11", "owner": "triciajthomas", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18366456547088091, "text": "One more reason to love Boots", "created_at": "2025-11-19T19:24:51", "owner": "semimetic", "likes": 4}, {"id": 18545476882031724, "text": "This is silly — M&S didn’t “invent” packaged sandwiches in 1980. I remember them from the 1960s in America, in exactly the same kind of packaging. In New Orleans, the local brand, Mrs. Drake’s, goes back to the 1930s. https://www.myneworleans.com/mrs-drake-days/", "created_at": "2025-11-24T06:31:38", "owner": "kikinola", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18149282992425673, "text": "A do like a meal deal. Tesco meal deals are ok, I particularly like their subs.", "created_at": "2025-11-30T11:43:04", "owner": "_alwaysabbie", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17898216207345844, "text": "Boots also had better meal deals than M&S. This is how I managed to push through with my Master's thesis at Cambridge 😅", "created_at": "2025-11-18T23:56:06", "owner": "vicnorgren", "likes": 13}, {"id": 18349359178166420, "text": "Sooner or later this will be a question on the British citizenship test", "created_at": "2025-11-22T23:13:49", "owner": "mar.murin", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18186527053343663, "text": "Boots may have invented the meal deal but M&S invented “dine in for 2 for £10” and that (along with a revamp of their food) basically saved the company", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:05:12", "owner": "got_a_beardo", "likes": 332}, {"id": 17864816727437588, "text": "I have no idea why they haven't spread across the globe! A meal deal would go down so well in Australia", "created_at": "2025-11-20T13:41:12", "owner": "fiishiing", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18080416897919732, "text": "All about getting the best bang for your buck! Grab those premium smoothies and desserts", "created_at": "2025-12-11T18:04:52", "owner": "britsnacksdotcom", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17862559140531865, "text": "Boots meal deal was mega in the 2000s", "created_at": "2025-11-20T02:49:29", "owner": "mattadoyle", "likes": 3}, {"id": 18093802183938490, "text": "73 meal deal a year in avg ! Do the maths agal bc it seem largely inflated number or on a very small panel", "created_at": "2025-12-17T19:21:54", "owner": "legrandchristo", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18424957414119420, "text": "For years living in London and I had none of them. Proud of keeping my spanish healthy meals ❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-30T01:18:41", "owner": "mel_siverio", "likes": 3}, {"id": 18065752457124224, "text": "The fact that such an unhealthy meal comes from a pharmacy is both surprising and not so surprising 😐 (they need costumers after all!)", "created_at": "2025-11-24T16:51:57", "owner": "gelsy_sleep_educator_ita", "likes": 7}, {"id": 18029889035558477, "text": "Love that", "created_at": "2025-12-03T11:00:34", "owner": "reallygoodenglishclasses", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18083305193292352, "text": "You bought sandwiches that weren't pre-packaged before M&S came up with the pre-packaged ones. They were made in the shop, restaurant, cafe or bakery that morning so we're a lot fresher and not on bread designed to last for days. When I first started working I used to often buy mine in Woolworths, they were in a brown paper bag. Simple choices like tinned salmon & cucumber, egg salad, ham & tomato or cheese and pickle. You could also go into Italian restaurants and they'd do you a fresh toastie. In all honesty they were much better.", "created_at": "2025-11-17T21:04:40", "owner": "merry_pepper_saffy", "likes": 14}, {"id": 18082982297032734, "text": "England without Meal Deal is like France with the Eiffel tower", "created_at": "2025-12-10T20:40:43", "owner": "marcelitanewton", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18075347312218187, "text": "Seeing british sandwich \"lunches\" is ussually the moment when a visitor from other european country is kind of glad to not live there.", "created_at": "2025-11-20T17:08:08", "owner": "lydiaquarck", "likes": 72}, {"id": 17856692043504163, "text": "Boots. There I saved you several minutes of waffle", "created_at": "2025-11-18T01:56:54", "owner": "sumobabypics", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18310790887188548, "text": "This is not real lunch. And it’s so sad people eat this rather then proper food.", "created_at": "2025-11-20T19:46:34", "owner": "2608.erica", "likes": 7}, {"id": 17866311336436828, "text": "Things that British museum was supposed to be filled with", "created_at": "2025-12-07T01:30:24", "owner": "armanalishahiha", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17939810778092738, "text": "Also the only country in the world where eating crisps is considered having a meal. I'll never get it 🤷🏼‍♀️😬", "created_at": "2025-11-20T06:10:11", "owner": "panic.and.freakout", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18393274483132046, "text": "The 1980s was also the decade that obesity rates starting to increase dramatically. 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-19T23:34:06", "owner": "weirdlyworldwide", "likes": 5}, {"id": 17971201619968263, "text": "Ahhh. Real ones know that the Boots one was the top tier original back in the day.\n\nThen came along Tesco and smashed it out of the park 🔥", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:24:28", "owner": "djwilxx", "likes": 45}, {"id": 18545758693043290, "text": "Meal deals were so handy for me during postgrad at Edinburgh - lived off of the Tesco chicken caesar wraps during my final paper all-nighters! 🙌", "created_at": "2025-11-18T22:45:37", "owner": "agarvin2014", "likes": 8}, {"id": 18074287445011986, "text": "It helps brazilian tourists", "created_at": "2025-11-28T17:27:10", "owner": "renata.bloz", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18327517387213708, "text": "One of the greatest inventions 👏❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-26T23:59:05", "owner": "albertocm_ldn", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17896100697349934, "text": "I make my own version so much cheaper and better for the money 💷", "created_at": "2025-11-27T05:21:51", "owner": "grievelb1980", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18083933195079247, "text": "In Australian I occasionally see packaged sandwiches in a petrol station but haven’t bought them in more than 10 years (but was a regular meal deal buyer before I left the UK in 2007).", "created_at": "2025-11-25T21:34:30", "owner": "chris.p.bacon76", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18057102356304962, "text": "How I miss that ❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-25T20:02:40", "owner": "gukolonko", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18096132292829142, "text": "This was amazing when I visited and the US needs meal deals too.", "created_at": "2025-11-25T18:20:56", "owner": "becspresso", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17884833756286524, "text": "Sainsbury’s is a rip off compared to most supermarket charging £4.30 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-25T00:57:23", "owner": "pixel53574", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18134891680466239, "text": "Spent 3 weeks in UK and I only had this for lunch.", "created_at": "2025-11-22T03:46:16", "owner": "lajavisilva", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18051213620362116, "text": "The UK must be the only country in the world that not only does these supermarket meal deals but also whose inhabitants eats crisps with a sandwich. Far too many carbs in one meal for my liking!", "created_at": "2025-11-17T22:47:35", "owner": "jmcgvino", "likes": 6}, {"id": 18066788411109475, "text": "Thank God for Prêt a Manger", "created_at": "2025-11-24T17:21:09", "owner": "lucianamiari", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18136573147418447, "text": "Unsung icon which is so unhealthy …", "created_at": "2025-11-24T11:50:07", "owner": "scotsgirl58", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18180332257359832, "text": "Che tristezza.... eat some good pasta instead 😂😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-23T23:12:24", "owner": "the_real_mrstodd", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18089680538496151, "text": "❤️ @bootsuk", "created_at": "2025-11-23T16:46:56", "owner": "besmartgetfit", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18098841451794274, "text": "The Boots in Leeds city centre also used to sell CDs at that time.", "created_at": "2025-11-23T17:27:39", "owner": "annacalewrites", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18047887862436335, "text": "😂👏", "created_at": "2025-11-22T23:13:33", "owner": "londonfashiontoday", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18545960185036877, "text": "@stgilesresident this is so true 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-23T02:10:53", "owner": "rio_damar", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18184555165352252, "text": "now it’s like £5+😢", "created_at": "2025-11-22T11:10:24", "owner": "idswhatever", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17936309369982098, "text": "I love it", "created_at": "2025-11-22T11:50:53", "owner": "naveda.rossana", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18080557559142953, "text": "the shock when I moved from Brazil to England and found out this was considered lunch 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-20T13:55:53", "owner": "annssantos", "likes": 454}, {"id": 18367115716084822, "text": "How did i work at boots head office for 5 years and not know they invented the meal deal?", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:02:22", "owner": "drunkatthehelm", "likes": 45}, {"id": 17934600339109967, "text": "😮😍🙌", "created_at": "2025-12-16T10:19:09", "owner": "angelaaachy", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18059805920640314, "text": "The meal deal saved us almost every day in our trip to London last October. For a family of 5 walking around to know the city, the meal deal was a great option!", "created_at": "2025-11-21T01:53:06", "owner": "melusachetto", "likes": 4}, {"id": 17936491886981830, "text": "Boots used to do a lovely chicken tikka flatbread, and a fizzy boysenberry drink in their meal deal. Good old days!", "created_at": "2025-11-24T15:09:22", "owner": "oratrixvo", "likes": 3}, {"id": 17989324322738771, "text": "£2,50 26 years ago and it's only about £4 now that's pretty good going", "created_at": "2025-11-18T10:25:11", "owner": "ushmiaster", "likes": 16}, {"id": 18096966739895086, "text": "I use to love boots meal deals 😍😍", "created_at": "2025-12-17T03:16:45", "owner": "its_pawsible_walkies", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17891224971240360, "text": "Boots still have the best meal deal", "created_at": "2025-11-22T09:38:02", "owner": "sativalikesalma", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18378135940199268, "text": "So happy to be italian 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-18T23:08:20", "owner": "marco0piras", "likes": 154}, {"id": 18144583543445645, "text": "Meal deal was invented by Boots Assistant to the Regional Manager in 1856; Sir Mealy Mc Dealey when he incorrectly put a 3 for 1 sticker and the public refused to allow the error to be corrected.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T08:30:18", "owner": "ahmed_shahid.jpg", "likes": 182}, {"id": 17903793546301414, "text": "😂😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-30T02:23:57", "owner": "radiantnavin", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17891492427368513, "text": "It’s the most depressing lunch I can imagine", "created_at": "2025-11-21T11:21:22", "owner": "yaron.einav", "likes": 7}, {"id": 17985721331919796, "text": "This information should be part of the Life in The UK test. 😂❤️", "created_at": "2025-12-17T11:30:23", "owner": "manololpez", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17955291093035091, "text": "Boots used to do a Mexican sarney with cheese and I don’t know what …I loved it …I think they ran a competition to invent new sandwich fillers !!", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:05:40", "owner": "mzfit123", "likes": 10}, {"id": 18330316756241925, "text": "Landing at Heathrow the other day I knew I was home when walking past Boots I saw those two words!", "created_at": "2025-12-04T20:18:03", "owner": "philthomas5036", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18081048929333940, "text": "I spent $15 on a sandwich today. Meal Deals are the best thing ever. Really keeps my UK travel budget down.", "created_at": "2025-11-22T06:06:09", "owner": "kiasuchick", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18074963531191805, "text": "It took off during the 80s because lunch at home had stopped being a thing with women having a significant presence in the workforce and more people eating their lunch at their desk. More labour and less leisure leads to increased demand for convenience foods", "created_at": "2025-11-18T07:27:59", "owner": "janellelizabeth89", "likes": 122}, {"id": 18044448257490252, "text": "Brilliant. But still not lunch 😂", "created_at": "2025-12-13T20:00:40", "owner": "astronaths", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18010694606806243, "text": "I travelled for a few weeks in the UK this summer and loved the meal deal! I’ve been telling my friends how essential it was to my travels!!! 😆 So funny!", "created_at": "2025-11-21T07:02:11", "owner": "triciajthomas", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18366456547088091, "text": "One more reason to love Boots", "created_at": "2025-11-19T19:24:51", "owner": "semimetic", "likes": 4}, {"id": 18545476882031724, "text": "This is silly — M&S didn’t “invent” packaged sandwiches in 1980. I remember them from the 1960s in America, in exactly the same kind of packaging. In New Orleans, the local brand, Mrs. Drake’s, goes back to the 1930s. https://www.myneworleans.com/mrs-drake-days/", "created_at": "2025-11-24T06:31:38", "owner": "kikinola", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18149282992425673, "text": "A do like a meal deal. Tesco meal deals are ok, I particularly like their subs.", "created_at": "2025-11-30T11:43:04", "owner": "_alwaysabbie", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17898216207345844, "text": "Boots also had better meal deals than M&S. This is how I managed to push through with my Master's thesis at Cambridge 😅", "created_at": "2025-11-18T23:56:06", "owner": "vicnorgren", "likes": 13}, {"id": 18349359178166420, "text": "Sooner or later this will be a question on the British citizenship test", "created_at": "2025-11-22T23:13:49", "owner": "mar.murin", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17864816727437588, "text": "I have no idea why they haven't spread across the globe! A meal deal would go down so well in Australia", "created_at": "2025-11-20T13:41:12", "owner": "fiishiing", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18080416897919732, "text": "All about getting the best bang for your buck! Grab those premium smoothies and desserts", "created_at": "2025-12-11T18:04:52", "owner": "britsnacksdotcom", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18186527053343663, "text": "Boots may have invented the meal deal but M&S invented “dine in for 2 for £10” and that (along with a revamp of their food) basically saved the company", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:05:12", "owner": "got_a_beardo", "likes": 332}, {"id": 17862559140531865, "text": "Boots meal deal was mega in the 2000s", "created_at": "2025-11-20T02:49:29", "owner": "mattadoyle", "likes": 3}, {"id": 18093802183938490, "text": "73 meal deal a year in avg ! Do the maths agal bc it seem largely inflated number or on a very small panel", "created_at": "2025-12-17T19:21:54", "owner": "legrandchristo", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18424957414119420, "text": "For years living in London and I had none of them. Proud of keeping my spanish healthy meals ❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-30T01:18:41", "owner": "mel_siverio", "likes": 3}, {"id": 18029889035558477, "text": "Love that", "created_at": "2025-12-03T11:00:34", "owner": "reallygoodenglishclasses", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18065752457124224, "text": "The fact that such an unhealthy meal comes from a pharmacy is both surprising and not so surprising 😐 (they need costumers after all!)", "created_at": "2025-11-24T16:51:57", "owner": "gelsy_sleep_educator_ita", "likes": 7}, {"id": 18083305193292352, "text": "You bought sandwiches that weren't pre-packaged before M&S came up with the pre-packaged ones. They were made in the shop, restaurant, cafe or bakery that morning so we're a lot fresher and not on bread designed to last for days. When I first started working I used to often buy mine in Woolworths, they were in a brown paper bag. Simple choices like tinned salmon & cucumber, egg salad, ham & tomato or cheese and pickle. You could also go into Italian restaurants and they'd do you a fresh toastie. In all honesty they were much better.", "created_at": "2025-11-17T21:04:40", "owner": "merry_pepper_saffy", "likes": 14}, {"id": 18082982297032734, "text": "England without Meal Deal is like France with the Eiffel tower", "created_at": "2025-12-10T20:40:43", "owner": "marcelitanewton", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18075347312218187, "text": "Seeing british sandwich \"lunches\" is ussually the moment when a visitor from other european country is kind of glad to not live there.", "created_at": "2025-11-20T17:08:08", "owner": "lydiaquarck", "likes": 72}, {"id": 17856692043504163, "text": "Boots. There I saved you several minutes of waffle", "created_at": "2025-11-18T01:56:54", "owner": "sumobabypics", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18310790887188548, "text": "This is not real lunch. And it’s so sad people eat this rather then proper food.", "created_at": "2025-11-20T19:46:34", "owner": "2608.erica", "likes": 7}, {"id": 17866311336436828, "text": "Things that British museum was supposed to be filled with", "created_at": "2025-12-07T01:30:24", "owner": "armanalishahiha", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17939810778092738, "text": "Also the only country in the world where eating crisps is considered having a meal. I'll never get it 🤷🏼‍♀️😬", "created_at": "2025-11-20T06:10:11", "owner": "panic.and.freakout", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18393274483132046, "text": "The 1980s was also the decade that obesity rates starting to increase dramatically. 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-19T23:34:06", "owner": "weirdlyworldwide", "likes": 5}, {"id": 17971201619968263, "text": "Ahhh. Real ones know that the Boots one was the top tier original back in the day.\n\nThen came along Tesco and smashed it out of the park 🔥", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:24:28", "owner": "djwilxx", "likes": 45}, {"id": 18545758693043290, "text": "Meal deals were so handy for me during postgrad at Edinburgh - lived off of the Tesco chicken caesar wraps during my final paper all-nighters! 🙌", "created_at": "2025-11-18T22:45:37", "owner": "agarvin2014", "likes": 8}, {"id": 18074287445011986, "text": "It helps brazilian tourists", "created_at": "2025-11-28T17:27:10", "owner": "renata.bloz", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18327517387213708, "text": "One of the greatest inventions 👏❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-26T23:59:05", "owner": "albertocm_ldn", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17896100697349934, "text": "I make my own version so much cheaper and better for the money 💷", "created_at": "2025-11-27T05:21:51", "owner": "grievelb1980", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18083933195079247, "text": "In Australian I occasionally see packaged sandwiches in a petrol station but haven’t bought them in more than 10 years (but was a regular meal deal buyer before I left the UK in 2007).", "created_at": "2025-11-25T21:34:30", "owner": "chris.p.bacon76", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18057102356304962, "text": "How I miss that ❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-25T20:02:40", "owner": "gukolonko", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18096132292829142, "text": "This was amazing when I visited and the US needs meal deals too.", "created_at": "2025-11-25T18:20:56", "owner": "becspresso", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17884833756286524, "text": "Sainsbury’s is a rip off compared to most supermarket charging £4.30 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-25T00:57:23", "owner": "pixel53574", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18134891680466239, "text": "Spent 3 weeks in UK and I only had this for lunch.", "created_at": "2025-11-22T03:46:16", "owner": "lajavisilva", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18051213620362116, "text": "The UK must be the only country in the world that not only does these supermarket meal deals but also whose inhabitants eats crisps with a sandwich. Far too many carbs in one meal for my liking!", "created_at": "2025-11-17T22:47:35", "owner": "jmcgvino", "likes": 6}, {"id": 18066788411109475, "text": "Thank God for Prêt a Manger", "created_at": "2025-11-24T17:21:09", "owner": "lucianamiari", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18136573147418447, "text": "Unsung icon which is so unhealthy …", "created_at": "2025-11-24T11:50:07", "owner": "scotsgirl58", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18180332257359832, "text": "Che tristezza.... eat some good pasta instead 😂😂😂", "created_at": "2025-11-23T23:12:24", "owner": "the_real_mrstodd", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18089680538496151, "text": "❤️ @bootsuk", "created_at": "2025-11-23T16:46:56", "owner": "besmartgetfit", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18098841451794274, "text": "The Boots in Leeds city centre also used to sell CDs at that time.", "created_at": "2025-11-23T17:27:39", "owner": "annacalewrites", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18047887862436335, "text": "😂👏", "created_at": "2025-11-22T23:13:33", "owner": "londonfashiontoday", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18545960185036877, "text": "@stgilesresident this is so true 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-23T02:10:53", "owner": "rio_damar", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18184555165352252, "text": "now it’s like £5+😢", "created_at": "2025-11-22T11:10:24", "owner": "idswhatever", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17936309369982098, "text": "I love it", "created_at": "2025-11-22T11:50:53", "owner": "naveda.rossana", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18348488029203470, "text": "Never bought a meal deal", "created_at": "2025-11-18T07:26:19", "owner": "helpsavemoney", "likes": 17}, {"id": 17915352279247462, "text": "Te va a encantar @lachicadeltour", "created_at": "2025-11-22T08:30:40", "owner": "ortheroad", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18160298881403290, "text": "😂", "created_at": "2025-11-21T22:12:06", "owner": "mp.f9158", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17992892987722518, "text": "If I think “meal deal” my brain automatically goes to the Boots fridge section. Even though I have never bought one and haven’t lived in the UK for over 20 years. 🧐", "created_at": "2025-11-21T14:16:30", "owner": "natalia082280", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17990423120900387, "text": "I assumed it was a copyycat of KFC  or some other fast food place", "created_at": "2025-11-21T02:38:45", "owner": "rockymcstar", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17914719411230176, "text": "How is crisps part of any meal? It’s carcinogenic", "created_at": "2025-11-20T22:56:09", "owner": "venividivronsky", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17927449653169593, "text": "Living off a meal deal is a sign it's time to switch up your life. Been there done it bought the t-shirt. Something you do in your 20s when you have disposable income, then you look back and realise how much money you wasted.", "created_at": "2025-11-20T23:41:55", "owner": "buckydoo", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17934841077101825, "text": "RIP M&S Salmon and Cucumber 🥺", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:05:52", "owner": "jollyhoscelyne", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18098253247829784, "text": "Being italian, me too I never understood why people would buy those sandwiches. The bread tasted like cardboard, the filling is also tasteless apart from the chicken and bacon ones. 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-20T11:02:51", "owner": "madameversiera", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18071100713586399, "text": "I worked at Boots in 1999 and remember stocking the £2.50 meal deal Shapers sarnies in the fridge. There was a triple decker chicken selection one that was the best value 🥪 to get in the deal 🤓 £1.95 with the staff discount which, at the time, also randomly included Halfords.", "created_at": "2025-11-18T00:09:26", "owner": "_dav_mac", "likes": 4}, {"id": 18207315601315658, "text": "I did not know things were this old", "created_at": "2025-11-20T00:10:34", "owner": "lovesandalwood", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18097222900757448, "text": "Nottingham: home of MRI and the meal deal (?)", "created_at": "2025-11-20T01:46:36", "owner": "repambrose", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18072543977349931, "text": "History I never thought I needed", "created_at": "2025-11-20T07:41:21", "owner": "ingloriousxbang", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17985046352915134, "text": "Glad to be very below average person with 0 consumption per year 😏🥳", "created_at": "2025-11-20T07:52:06", "owner": "roya.dera", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18139808323454364, "text": "What an amazing account this is. Learning so much from it, thank you!", "created_at": "2025-11-20T08:50:05", "owner": "thedancingtable", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17865299616502251, "text": "Impossible that nobody sold packaged sandwiches before the 1980s!", "created_at": "2025-11-19T17:03:07", "owner": "theledge80", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17873030505452238, "text": "\"miu-diu\" is my favourite word 😍💕✨", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:43:21", "owner": "_mr_dale", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18118982116551782, "text": "Love all day breakfast 😍", "created_at": "2025-11-19T21:16:04", "owner": "stepan.placak", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17884343700283218, "text": "And now all need to know how “meal deal tried to concour” the USA market and failed miserably - because indeed - people there just could not get the hype 😭😂", "created_at": "2025-11-19T19:25:54", "owner": "madlivilsar", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18088307921317937, "text": "Now somebody please bring these to Canada.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T19:51:46", "owner": "oldsheldon", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17901260268313853, "text": "2.99 in 1999. It is expensive if you compare it to todays rate as in Sainsbury's and Tesco you get a meal deal for just under 4 quids", "created_at": "2025-11-18T21:51:00", "owner": "sumeet__gupta", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17983173980760609, "text": "73 meal deals a year🫤, we need to strengthen NHS to cope with all that rectal cancer that is coming", "created_at": "2025-11-19T16:15:42", "owner": "dizziefizz", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17850244452595423, "text": "I had it at boots originally but didn't realise they were the first to sell it", "created_at": "2025-11-19T07:49:11", "owner": "natdowsett98", "likes": 3}, {"id": 17890324575381121, "text": "Keeps you going when you can’t stop but it’s not exactly healthy for you in the long term. Just Carbs and Sugar and a little protein.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T12:42:37", "owner": "roylyle1979", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17968606799976592, "text": "The power of marketing", "created_at": "2025-11-19T17:12:23", "owner": "thestorybudget", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18024400457773311, "text": "So unhealthy 😢", "created_at": "2025-11-19T13:18:16", "owner": "skyfeather_travels", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18061130651213854, "text": "Horrible and unhealthy with that awful bread", "created_at": "2025-11-19T13:45:20", "owner": "aracelijimenezb", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17866471794486445, "text": "my husband biggest hapinnes in the UK ist going to Tesco and get a meal Deal 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-19T14:21:56", "owner": "xispathegreat", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18086967919801585, "text": "“They couldn’t understand why anyone would buy one” this is the issue, the people in the head office are likely educated and logical, they forget that the general public are not.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T11:42:33", "owner": "joshfm.the.human", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18098136154693959, "text": "Yessss I REMEMBER now specifically getting a ‘Boots meal deal’! I’d forgotten the simple joy back then", "created_at": "2025-11-19T00:39:04", "owner": "atp86", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18088263272313716, "text": "Love TESCO !", "created_at": "2025-11-19T00:45:15", "owner": "soakdelatorre", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18183571363353345, "text": "So what were people eating at work before M&S 'invented' a 🥪", "created_at": "2025-11-19T03:23:58", "owner": "nancyshmansy", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18047410166428269, "text": "salute i never knew and im from the usa but loved getting them at tescos when we visited the uk", "created_at": "2025-11-19T05:14:48", "owner": "30recs", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18100300345736725, "text": "And of course the proper meal deal for Saturday night just dig out the Barry White records and you’re there 👍🏻", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:17:46", "owner": "dazz4979", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18033243017536510, "text": "Sainsbury's Meal deal is now £3.95 ! Horror!!!😡", "created_at": "2025-12-18T21:21:23", "owner": "hashtag_mister_france", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18382246309147604, "text": "I was surprised to see this meal deal all the rage when I was out there earlier this year. This isnt lunch it’s a snack.", "created_at": "2025-12-18T17:32:04", "owner": "stilljil_", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17853441534595499, "text": "Unhealthy and insipid.", "created_at": "2025-12-13T17:55:55", "owner": "mariagon_ag", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18080503201919405, "text": "Whoever invented, should be jailed for this. I am shocked by the amount of UPF people are able to eat. And I pay my tax to ensure free healthcare.", "created_at": "2025-12-10T17:35:22", "owner": "letiziamarchetti1", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18128549344447174, "text": "Guys, are you proud to consider this lunch? Our NHS will never keep up", "created_at": "2025-12-10T07:51:59", "owner": "letiziamarchetti1", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17919967398217514, "text": "@quinn_g08 😮", "created_at": "2025-12-04T22:20:04", "owner": "ch_rl_tt_g", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17977721099947243, "text": "It is literally the staple of British culture", "created_at": "2025-12-02T11:06:55", "owner": "thebrandanalyst", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18085298741314055, "text": "73 crikey that’s a lot", "created_at": "2025-12-02T09:45:41", "owner": "leithwalk_popups", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18094916383853430, "text": "73 of these in a year is diabolical", "created_at": "2025-12-01T23:52:06", "owner": "ivankhr_", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18086300956993655, "text": "I don’t and I am not fat 🍰", "created_at": "2025-11-27T14:54:56", "owner": "creativeworldcreative", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18193764919335168, "text": "People thought I was lying when I said boots invented the meal deal, I swear sometimes they had offers and meal deals could be as low as £1.50", "created_at": "2025-11-27T13:08:43", "owner": "brosef_ballin", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18085809586982185, "text": "Crap and label as a meal….", "created_at": "2025-11-27T00:45:04", "owner": "h3nrythe51nn3r_72", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17988952208740404, "text": "What were people eating before 1980?! Good lord, it doesn’t bear thinking.", "created_at": "2025-11-25T17:40:55", "owner": "i_am_pete81", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18331193857240593, "text": "@hannahwitton", "created_at": "2025-11-24T17:57:35", "owner": "erinherzog101", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18085696922285033, "text": "\"some shithole country\" said BoJo", "created_at": "2025-11-23T17:57:34", "owner": "ronettepolanski", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18086266702949019, "text": "I’m still trying to understand why anybody would buy one", "created_at": "2025-11-23T14:34:45", "owner": "bhartilbajaj", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18150062683420398, "text": "@estellamaria.x", "created_at": "2025-11-22T16:50:37", "owner": "jorvik_education", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17979349274783120, "text": "Meal deal is disgusting, so is the UK.", "created_at": "2025-11-21T09:20:40", "owner": "rodolphocr", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17914725873090633, "text": "And now it's £4.50 😢", "created_at": "2025-11-20T21:45:35", "owner": "anna_djd", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18101798935675328, "text": "Imagine colonising the whole world but your people consider this lunch", "created_at": "2025-11-20T21:34:10", "owner": "halasarabi6988", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17975905844940729, "text": "👏👏👏🔥🔥🔥 meal deal saved me so many times ey!!!!!", "created_at": "2025-11-20T20:22:02", "owner": "ywmnsa", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18330667798208767, "text": "Had quite a few of those cold lunches...even the crisps were cold 🥶", "created_at": "2025-11-20T19:03:34", "owner": "nausheenbushrah", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18085993471805255, "text": "Sad food", "created_at": "2025-11-20T17:50:01", "owner": "nejafeja", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18078793447918443, "text": "@wilbur.the.goat 👀", "created_at": "2025-11-20T11:47:07", "owner": "itsannachiara", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17978752058783513, "text": "Meal deal is the saddest thing in the UK, as if the weather wasn't enough to make you miserable", "created_at": "2025-11-20T11:31:59", "owner": "dianitamarcelap", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18058445747274854, "text": "So sad", "created_at": "2025-11-20T09:19:38", "owner": "gilgameshspqr", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18082921342849792, "text": "@jigeumeun I’m excited for meal deal", "created_at": "2025-11-20T07:06:08", "owner": "suzanne_tham", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17852567139583418, "text": "Colonized all those countries and still eating terrible food daily 👏", "created_at": "2025-11-20T05:29:16", "owner": "marianatravels", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18366013192088230, "text": "Back in 1979/80 my grandma Shirley was part of a small team of ladies who started making the tester M&S pre-packed sandwiches fresh by hand in a small factory in NW London early every morning. I remember her talking about how they had to make sure the filling went right to the edges. Once the lunchtime sandwich concept was successful & M&S decided they would be a staple food product, all the ladies were offered jobs in any M&S they wanted on the foods department. My grandma chose Kensington High Street. She worked there for the next 20 years & loved it 🥰 🩵", "created_at": "2025-11-19T22:20:55", "owner": "phillippa1973", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18063648071171957, "text": "@kalanighosthunter", "created_at": "2025-11-19T20:22:31", "owner": "emma2white", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18207875659312732, "text": "Protestant countries have a very toxic relationship with food. Since you decided that good quality properly cooked food was Catholic and inefficient you condemned yourself to a horrible life.", "created_at": "2025-11-19T19:41:48", "owner": "nicolas.pineda.salazar", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17851927404584249, "text": "Looking forward to a future deep dive into the history of Luncheon Vouchers (too niché?)", "created_at": "2025-11-19T17:31:47", "owner": "begleybegley", "likes": 2}, {"id": 18398365237127960, "text": "Most unhealthy\"food\"  you can put in your body", "created_at": "2025-11-19T16:49:57", "owner": "lavidadeedu", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18029951927546842, "text": "Poor British people", "created_at": "2025-11-19T15:28:53", "owner": "niuhui_00", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18101057311685916, "text": "Terrible 😢 i love being in mexico now", "created_at": "2025-11-19T07:05:22", "owner": "jamiefatale", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18060795128200446, "text": "73 on avg?! I get them almost every day lol.", "created_at": "2025-11-18T15:15:09", "owner": "pranav_desu", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18112214821597587, "text": "Oooh I didn’t know that it was Boots. I LOVE a boots meal deal esp when im skint", "created_at": "2025-11-18T12:03:23", "owner": "gwenjbrewer", "likes": 1}, {"id": 17940298301960327, "text": "@ale_carabo", "created_at": "2025-11-18T10:26:34", "owner": "prof_scorp", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18012324050637734, "text": "❤️❤️❤️", "created_at": "2025-11-18T02:38:03", "owner": "kimiklown", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18057603668277252, "text": "Boots All Day Breakfast  on Baked Bean Bread used to be yer full Calories intake for the day!! Strangely it's no longer available......", "created_at": "2025-11-18T00:42:32", "owner": "steven_dewar", "likes": 1}, {"id": 18063159293427311, "text": "Always get the most expensive in the 3 categories 😂", "created_at": "2025-11-18T00:03:06", "owner": "meyta_mechta", "likes": 0}, {"id": 17925566772173759, "text": "The meal deals is a 6.3 billion pound industry thats wild", "created_at": "2025-11-17T23:25:11", "owner": "master_moses_keys", "likes": 0}, {"id": 18050214770375190, "text": "Tesco and co-slop sandwiches - utter garbage.", "created_at": "2025-11-17T23:03:00", "owner": "tedsbarbernomad", "likes": 2}, {"id": 17887569045264431, "text": "Brits have the taste buds of a mosquito. This stuff is disgusting.", "created_at": "2025-11-17T20:32:18", "owner": "delavega1849", "likes": 3}, {"id": 18001271483829547, "text": "The average person? 73? So 52 weeks in a year = 1.4 a week. Or 73/12 so 6.1 a month. Really? Hmm people are mental", "created_at": "2025-11-17T19:53:53", "owner": "chrisfliverpool", "likes": 0}], "location": null, "hashtags": ["british", "britishicon", "britishculture", "britishlife", "britishfood", "mealdeal", "mealdeals"]},
